From a6bbb3236c99678fe7305c1019b228c609db534b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: huying <huying21@huawei.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Mar 2026 17:10:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ums: fix and prevent credits deadlock by reserving emergency
 credits

Description:
To prevent potential deadlock scenarios in credit exchange, this PR
introduces an emergency credit reservation mechanism and fixes a credit
leak.

1. Reserve emergency credits: When both sides reach zero peer_rq_credits,
they cannot announce new credits to each other. This patch reserves
emergency credits specifically for LLC_ANNOUNCE_CREDITS messages to
break this cycle.
2. Fix credit leak: In ums_tx_ub_write_imm, credits acquired via
ums_get_imm were not returned if ubcore_post_jetty_send_wr failed. This
leak is now fixed by ensuring credits are returned via
ums_wr_rx_put_credits on failure paths.

Key changes:
 - ums_wr.h: add ums_wr_tx_get_credit_emergency for emergency mode
 - ums_wr.h: modify ums_wr_tx_get_credit to reserve emergency credits
 - ums_wr.c: add emergency parameter to ums_wr_tx_get_free_slot
 - ums_llc.c: use emergency=true only for ums_llc_announce_credits
 - ums_cdc.c: CDC/IMM use normal mode (emergency=false)
 - ums_tx.c: add u8 *credits output parameter to ums_get_imm function
 - ums_tx.c: return credits via ums_wr_rx_put_credits when post send fails

(cherry picked from commit 9b27a8f024fa85d491c07f1119b417c5eca2387d)
